WEB APIs

Web APIs let frontend developers access browser features and external services directly from JavaScript. You can change the DOM, make network requests, store data, manage media, and enable real-time communication. They are crucial for creating dynamic and interactive web applications.

Key APIs  
- DOM API: Access and manipulate HTML and CSS elements.  
- Fetch API / XMLHttpRequest: Make HTTP requests to retrieve or send data from or to servers.  
- Storage APIs: Use LocalStorage, SessionStorage, and IndexedDB for client-side data storage.  
- Canvas & WebGL: Draw graphics, animations, and interactive content.  
- Geolocation API: Access user location with permission for location-based features.  
- Web Sockets and Server-Sent Events: Real-time communication with servers.  
- Notification API: Show system notifications to users.  
- Web Audio and Video APIs: Handle media playback and manipulation.  

